{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792712131,"nonce":"ehHgYHin2pCU8nmDtzRRzASuvxU=","target":"dc742c2e7d0a18bfff8ce06f4bfb92ddaa67887fd1564dd8eca0729831b9b57c","message":"Every compiled loop header in the Cranelift baseline loads the arm byte and branches, so a loop can move to a helper a higher tier publishes. With the default ladder (`zynode run`, no `--llvm`) nothing above the baseline ever publishes one, so the load and branch run every iteration for nothing.\n\nChange: `loop_probes(config)` in `zyntax_embed/src/runtime/tiered.rs` decides the setting for all three `set_emit_osr_probes` sites. Probes are emitted only when OSR is enabled and LLVM is the selected top tier. `ZYNTAX_BASELINE_OSR_PROBES=1` restores the old behaviour in the same binary; safe to run with.\n\nMeasurement: NUC (i5-1250P, x86-64), release build, whole-process wall time, interleaved A/B, minimum of 5, same binary with and without the env var, identical program output in every row.\n\n| kernel | probes on | probes off | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| fib(38) | 0.11 | 0.10 | 1.10 |\n| sieve 20M | 0.30 | 0.28 | 1.07 |\n| mandelbrot 2000 | 0.37 | 0.27 | 1.37 |\n| spectral 1000 | 0.08 | 0.08 | 1.00 |\n| fannkuch(10) | 0.56 | 0.52 | 1.08 |\n| nbody 3M | 0.07 | 0.06 | 1.17 |\n| k % 7, 100M | 0.20 | 0.19 | 1.05 |\n| k * 7, 100M | 0.19 | 0.06 | 3.17 |\n| 120 funcs, 20000 rounds | 0.86 | 0.43 | 2.00 |\n| fannkuch(9) | 0.07 | 0.05 | 1.40 |\n\nThe default tier now matches `--llvm` on mandelbrot and `k * 7`. The old doc comment on `enable_osr` claimed under 1% cost; it is replaced.\n\nOut of scope here: the Python and Lua frontends reach LLVM through the same config, so they keep probes exactly when LLVM is the top tier.\n\nRemaining default-tier gaps against Node on this machine: fannkuch(10) (float-index guard), 120 funcs (see 34cfd6f for the LLVM side).","files":null}]}